        "type": "text",
        "text": "You are a judge of syntactic circuits. Work only in the current folder.\n1. Read RULES.md completely, including every settled case at its end.\n2. Read packet-1.jsonl: each line {n, text, sop} is a message and one circuit written for it by a formalizer that saw only the words of that message.\n3. Judge every line by RULES.md and write verdicts-1.jsonl in this folder, one JSON line per packet line: {\"n\": <number>, \"grade\": \"L8\" or \"L1\"..\"L6\", \"note\": \"<one sentence>\"}. L8 accepts. For a rejection the note must quote the words of the message in single quotes and name the wrong statement or the lost information; if you cannot quote one, the circuit is acceptable.\n4. Run: node check.mjs 1   and fix whatever it reports until it passes.\nWork in batch: read the whole packet, then write the whole verdicts file at once (you may write it in a few large parts); do not edit line by line. Judge fairly: a plausible or incomplete reading that the next layer can continue from is acceptable; reject only a wrong statement or lost explicit information. Do not edit any other file."
      }
    ],
