\"a bit\" as a nominal — but as a COMPLEMENT of \"want\"? \"I want a bit\" — states wanting a bit — wrong. Hmm — \"want the bench a bit closer\" — \"a bit closer\" — \"closer\" is modifier of clause (grading), \"a bit\" measure nominal. The circuit: c1 modifier \"closer\", complements n2 (bench) and n3 (\"a bit\") — \"I want the long bench and a bit\" — two things wanted — wrong: \"a bit\" is not wanted; it measures \"closer\". Per the settled time-phrase case analog (coordination with what the verb acts on states a second thing acted on: L3) — here a second complement — L3-ish. But L1 comes first for c2's form. Grade L1, note about \"leave\". Or should the note be about \"a bit\"? First applicable grade: L1 (c2 declarative command). I'll go L1 with note on 'leave'.\n\n**n=95**: \"right, for readers who skim I'd like the first paragraph moved before the chapter heading, with the remaining blocks in order\"\n- c1 declarative discourse \"right\" auxiliary \"'d\" verb \"like\" subject n2 (\"I\"). r1 \"for\" from c1 to n1 (\"readers\"). r2 \"who\" from n1 to c2 (\"skim\"). n3 \"the first paragraph\". c3 nonfinite \"moved\" subject n3. r3 \"before\" from c3 to n4 (\"the chapter heading\"). r4 \"with\" from c3 to c4 (fragment complement n5 \"the remaining blocks\"). r5 \"in\" from n5 to n6 (\"order\"). r6 from c1 to c3.\n- \"right,\" at start — discourse — fine. \"for readers who skim\" — r1 \"for\" from c1 to \"readers\", r2 \"who\" from readers to c2 — fine. \"I'd like the first paragraph moved before the chapter heading\" — c1 \"I'd like\" + c3 nonfinite \"moved\" subject \"the first paragraph\", tied r6 from c1. \"with the remaining blocks in order\" — r4 \"with\" from c3 to c4 fragment — fine. L8.\n\n**n=96**: \"create a timeline of the hiring rounds, left to right, with even gaps between the ticks\"\n- c1 imperative \"create\" complement n1 (\"a timeline\"). r1 \"of\" from n1 to n2 (\"the hiring rounds\"). n3 \"left\". r2 \"to\" from n3 to n4 (\"right\"). r3 \"with\" (ambiguous) from c1 to n5 (\"even gaps\"). r4 \"between\" from n5 to n6 (\"the ticks\"). r5 from n1 to n3.\n- \"left to right\" — n3 \"left\" tied from n1 (timeline), r2 \"to\" from left to \"right\" — \"left to right\" as a direction phrase — decomposed — fine. L8.\n\n**n=97**: \"a little bird up in the top right, then place the green block one space left and a quarter space up but never touching the blue block, no other change, so the spacing comes out even\"\n- n1 \"a little bird\". c1 fragment modifier \"up\" complement n1. r1 \"in\" from c1 to n2 (\"the top right\"). k1 \"then\",\"and\",\"but\",\"so\" conjunct c1, c2, c5, c4. c2 imperative \"place\" modifiers \"left\",\"up\" complements n3 (\"the green block\"), n4 (\"one space\"), n5 (\"a quarter space\"). c3 nonfinite negation \"never\" verb \"touching\" complement n6 (\"the blue block\"). n7 \"no other change\". c4 declarative \"comes\" modifiers \"out\",\"even\" subject n8 (\"the spacing\"). r2 from c2 to c3. c5 fragment complement n7.\n- Issues: k1 has four conjunctions (\"then\",\"and\",\"but\",\"so\") with conjuncts c1, c2, c5, c4 — the message: \"a little bird up in the top right, then place ... one space left and a quarter space up but never touching the blue block, no other change, so the spacing comes out even\". The conjunctions: \"then\" (bird→place), \"and\" (left and a quarter space up — between modifiers!), \"but\" (but never touching), \"so\" (so the spacing comes out). Hmm — \"and\" is between \"one space left\" and \"a quarter space up\" — both parts of the place command — the circuit has \"and\" as a conjunction of k1 joining... the conjuncts c1, c2, c5, c4 with conjunctions then/and/but/so — messy: \"but never touching the blue block\" — c3 (touching) is tied via r2 from c2 — but the \"but\" conjunction in k1 — k1's conjuncts don't include c3! The \"but\" is used in k1 but c3 is not a conjunct — c3 is tied by r2 (no marker) from c2. Hmm — \"but never touching\" — \"but\" should join c3 (t