(\"it\"). r3 \"from\" from c5 to n10 (\"there\"). c6 declarative \"make\" modifier \"bigger\" complements n11 (\"the font\"), n12 (\"a bit\"). k1 \"and\",\"so\",\"and\",\"and\" conjunct c1, c2, c4, c5, c6. r4 from c2 to c3.\n- Issues: (a) c6 \"and make the font a bit bigger\" — declarative with no subject — per the settled case (verb after \"and\" following a clause with subject and auxiliary \"'ll\") — \"I'll take it from there, and make the font a bit bigger\" — \"make\" shares \"I'll\" → nonfinite/declarative no subject — passes (like n=138). (b) \"make the lines ... distinct colours\" — \"distinct colours\" as complement — \"colours\" head with \"distinct\" dependent — fine. (c) k1 with 5 conjuncts — same as 138 — fine. L8.\n\n**n=143**: \"when the regions dial in tomorrow the first chart they see is Claims by month, so for their sake make the markers black before the meeting starts, and give it the title Claims history\"\n- r1 \"when\" from c3 to c1. n1 \"the regions\". c1 declarative \"dial\" modifiers in/tomorrow subject n1. n2 \"the first chart\". n3 \"they\". c2 declarative \"see\" subject n3. c3 declarative \"is\" subject n2 complement n4 (\"Claims\"). r2 \"by\" from n4 to n5 (\"month\"). r3 \"so\" from c3 to k1. r4 \"for\" from c4 to n6 (\"their sake\"). c4 imperative \"make\" modifier \"black\" complement n7 (\"the markers\"). r5 \"before\" from c4 to c5 (\"starts\" subject \"the meeting\"). k1 \"and\" conjunct c4, c6. c6 imperative \"give\" complements n9 (\"it\"), n10 (\"the title\"). n11 \"Claims history\". r6 n2→c2. r7 n10→n11.\n- \"so for their sake make the markers black before the meeting starts, and give it the title Claims history\" — k1 \"and\" joins c4 (make) and c6 (give) — the message's \"and\" is between \"starts\" and \"give\" — joins make... and give... — fine. r3 \"so\" from c3 to k1 — the so-relation ends at the coordination — fine. L8.\n\n**n=144**: \"and also let's restore the arrow size to one step smaller\"\n- c1 imperative discours