lace word as dependent of nominal — allowed. L8.\n\n**n=147**: \"Don't keep them on screen, but flash the IDs quickly so I can note the diamond's\"\n- c1 imperative auxiliary \"Do\" negation \"n't\" verb \"keep\" complement n1 (\"them\"). r1 \"on\" from c1 to n2 (\"screen\"). k1 \"but\" conjunct c1, c2. c2 imperative \"flash\" modifier \"quickly\" complement n3 (\"the IDs\"). r2 \"so\" from c2 to c3 (\"can note\" subject \"I\" complement n5). n5 \"the diamond's\" — head \"diamond\" dependent \"'s\".\n- \"the diamond's\" — \"'s\" as dependent of \"diamond\" — the possessive marker as dependent — settled: \"'s\" is a marker... \"the marker is the linking word: a preposition, \"'s\", ...\" — \"'s\" held as a dependent of the nominal — L3: \"A linking word is held as a modifier or a dependent.\" Hmm — \"the diamond's\" — \"'s\" is the possessive 's — within a nominal \"the diamond's\" — is \"'s\" a linking word here? \"the diamond's\" — the 's attaches to diamond — in the schema, \"'s\" is listed as a marker (linking word) — e.g. \"the box's colour\" — relation marker \"'s\" from box to colour. Here the message ends at \"the diamond's\" — no following noun — so \"'s\" has nothing to link to — held as dependent of \"diamond\" — since there's no second nominal, \"'s\" standing in the nominal is... the word must stand somewhere. Held as dependent — plausible (the possessive as part of the nominal). I'll accept. L8.\n\n**n=148**: \"and again — build a green column between the purple columns, exactly three blocks tall, and then put one blue block on top of each purple tower\"\n- c1 imperative discourse \"and\" modifier \"again\" verb \"build\" modifier \"tall\" complements n1 (\"a green column\"), n3 (\"exactly three blocks\"). r1 \"between\" from n1 to n2 (\"the purple columns\"). n3: dependents exactly/three, head \"blocks\". k1 \"and\" conjunct c1, c2. c2 imperative modifier \"then\" verb \"put\" complement n4 (\"one blue block\"). r2 \"on\" from c2 to n5 (\"top\"). r3 \"